    "ls|LS16_S6_U_120": "1 \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 120 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2015 \n \nKENDRIYA VIDYALAYAS/NAVODAYA VIDYALAYAS \n \n*120.  SHRI TAMRADHWAJ SAHU:  \nSHRI RAJESHBHAI CHUDASAMA:  \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOUR CE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a)  the details of the ex isting Kendriya Vidyalayas , Navodaya Vidyalayas and \nKasturba Gandhi Balika Vidyalayas in the country, State/UT-wise;  \n(b) the seats available for students and sanctioned po sts for teachers in the \nsaid schools, State/UT-wise;  \n(c)  whether the existing number of Ke ndriya Vidyalayas, Navodaya Vidyalayas \nand Kasturba Gandhi Balika Vidyalayas are not sufficient to cater to the demand \nand if so, the details thereof; and  \n(d)  whether the Government is considering to increase  the number of the said \nVidyalayas in the country and if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise along with \nthe time frame set to achieve the target? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n \n  \n\n2 \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO  PARTS (a) TO (d) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 12 0 RAISED BY SHRI TAMRADHWAJ \nSAHU & SHRI RAJESHBHAI CHUD ASAMA, HON’BLE MPs TO BE \nANSWERED ON 7th DECEMBER 2015 REGARDING KENDRIYA VIDYALAYAS/ \nNAVODAYA VIDYALAYAS. \n \n(a) & (b) Details of the State/UT wise number of Kendriya Vidyalayas (KVs), \nJawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas (JNVs) and Kasturba Gandhi Balika Vidyalayas \n(KGBVs) in the country alongwith the seats available for students and the total \nsanctioned posts of teachers in these Vidyalayas are annexed.  \n \n(c) & (d) Proposals for opening of new KVs are considered only if sponsored by \nMinistries or Departments of the Governm ent of India, State Governments / Union \nTerritories Administrations or  Organization of employees  belonging to the eligible \ncategories thereby committing resources for setting up a new KV as well as on the \navailability of necessary sanction of the Government. Navodaya Vidyalaya \nScheme provides for opening of one Jawahar Navodaya Vi dyalaya (JNV) in each \ndistrict of the country. O pening of KVs and JNVs is a continuous process which \ndepends upon approval by co mpetent authority, avai lability of funds and \navailability of suitable land free of cost from the s ponsoring agency as well as \navailability of rent free te mporary accommodation to oper ationalise the Vidyalaya. \nAs such, no time frame can be set for opening of KVs and JNVs.  \n  \nThe KGBV scheme provides for setting up  of one residential upper primary \nschool for girls from SC,S T,OBC and minority communities in each educational \nbackward block (EBB) subject to cert ain conditions. As many as 3609 KGBVs \nhave been sanctioned in the country and 3598 are operational . There are seats \nstill available in the existing KGBVs. As such, at present, there is no immediate \nproposal for opening of new KGBVs.    \n****** \n  \n\n3 \n \nANNEXURE \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 120 RAISED BY SHRI TAMRADHWAJ SAHU & SHRI RAJESHBHAI CHUDASAMA, HON’BLE MPs \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 7 th DECEMBER 2015 REGARDING KEND RIYA VIDYALAYAS/ NAVODAYA \nVIDYALAYAS \n \nSTATE WISE NUMBER OF KVs, JNVs AND KGBV s IN THE COUNTRY ALONG WITH THE TOTAL \nSANCTIONED AS WELL AS ACTUAL STRENGTH OF TEACHERS IN THESE VIDYALAYAS \nSr. \nN. \nName of State \nKendriya Vidyalayas \nJawahar Navodaya \nVidyalayas \nKasturba Gandhi Balika \nVidyalayas \n  No. of \nVidya-\nlayas  \nseats \navailable \nfor \nadmission \nSanc-\ntioned \npost of \nteachers \nNo. of \nVidya-\nlayas \nSeats \navailable \nfor \nstudents  \nSanc-\ntioned \npost of \nteachers  \nNo. of \nVidya-\nlayas \nseats \navailable \nfor \nadmission \nSanc-\ntioned