    "ls|LS16_S6_U_99": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 99\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.12.2015\nAGITATION IN FTII\n*99: SHRI S.R. VIJAYAKUMAR:\nSHRI JYOTIRADITYA M. SCINDIA:\nWill the Minister of lnformation and Broadcasting be pleased to state:\na) the details of norms/guidelines for the appointment of the President of Film and\nTelevision Institute of India (FTll);\nb) whether the students of FTll were on long strike over the issue, if so, the\nreasons therefor along with details of their demands;\nc) the extent to which curriculum is likely to be affected as a result of students\nstrike; and\nd) whether the Government has taken any step to resolve the issue and find an\namicable solution in the matter and if so, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nTHE MlNlsrER oF FINANGE; MlNlsrER oF coRPoRATE AFFATRS; AND\nMINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING (SHRI ARUN JAITLEY)\n(a) to (d) A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n\nSTATEMENT AS REFERRED TO lN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) OF THE LOK\nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO 99 TO BE ANSWERED ON 4.12.2015\nThe appointment in Film and Television lnstitute of lndia (FTll), Pune is governed as\nper the set of provisions of Film and Television lnstitute of India (FTll) Rules. As per\nRule 3 (1) of FTll Rules, President of the Institute is nominated by the Central\nGovernment.\nThe students of FTll were on strike for some time. The reasons for the agitation as\nstated by the students are inclusion of some members, including the President, in the\nnewly constituted society of the Institute.\nNo academic activity happened during the period of protest which has a bearing on\ncourse completion of already delayed batches of FTll.\nTo resolve the issues and to bring normalcy in the lnstitute, the Ministry made sincere\neffortswith 7 rounds of discussions held on 03.07.2015,06.08.2015 ,29.09.2015,\n01.10.2015 , 07.10.2015 ,10.10.2015 & 20.10.2015 with the FTll Students'Association\nand alumni of FTll at all levels in the Ministry.\nThe students of FTll called off their strike on 28.10.2015.\n****"
